The HL7 v2.5.1 reference data ships in the hl7v2-core package (core/).

The files in core/data/ are generated by core/scripts/generate.mjs from the sources
below. Each record carries a `src` object naming where each attribute came from.

1. HAPI HL7v2 structures for v2.5.1
   ca.uhn.hapi:hapi-structures-v251:2.5.1 and ca.uhn.hapi:hapi-base:2.5.1
   https://hapifhir.github.io/hapi-hl7v2/
   Licence: Mozilla Public License 1.1 OR GNU General Public License (dual).
   Used for: segment and field definitions (names, data types, lengths,
   repetition, R/O optionality, ID/IS table bindings), composite data type
   components, message structures (groups, choices) and the trigger-event to
   structure map. No HAPI code is included; the extracted definitions describe
   the HL7 v2.5.1 standard. If your redistribution policy treats extracted
   definitions as covered by the MPL, the MPL 1.1 terms apply to core/data/.

2. HL7 Terminology (THO), package hl7.terminology.r4 version 7.4.0
   https://terminology.hl7.org/
   Licence: CC0-1.0.
   Used for: table names and types, code displays and definitions, and the
   "where used" property that supplies CE/CWE table bindings HAPI lacks
   (tagged "THO v2-where-used" in the data, because THO reflects the latest v2
   version).

3. HL7 FHIR STU3 (3.0.2) v2 table pages, https://hl7.org/fhir/STU3/v2/
   Licence: CC0-1.0 (FHIR licence, https://hl7.org/fhir/STU3/license.html).
   Used for: the per-code version history (v2.1 to v2.8.2) that decides
   whether a code is valid in v2.5.1.

4. Curated overlay (core/data/overlay/*.json): implementation notes written by the
   project author, plus sourced corrections in core/data/overrides.json (each with
   its evidence).

